From 1e26010ba832484c968dbfa1702b5ca907c8e4da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:03:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] fix(scheduler): elect one worker to run APScheduler
 instead of every uvicorn worker

start_scheduler() ran unconditionally in each worker's lifespan, so with the
default --workers 4 every cron job executed four times: four
system_metrics_snapshots per hour (skewing the Operations dashboard), four
model syncs, four budget resets and four reconcile_drifted_reserved_counters
runs racing on the same rows.

app/services/scheduler_leader.py: leadership = pg_try_advisory_xact_lock
(id 56023115, sibling of the DDL/bootstrap locks in main.py) held inside an
open transaction on a dedicated connection. Holding it transactionally is what
makes it correct behind PgBouncer's transaction pooling: the open transaction
pins one server connection to this process for as long as it lives. The
leader heartbeats on that connection every 15s and steps down (stopping its
scheduler) when the heartbeat fails; non-leaders retry every 30s, so a dead
leader is replaced within about half a minute. SQLite: first caller leads.

main.py: SchedulerLeader with on_acquire=start_scheduler+schedule refreshes,
on_release=stop_scheduler; one synchronous attempt at startup so
single-worker deployments and tests behave as before, then the background
loop. The video worker stays on every worker: it claims with
FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED and is safe by design.

Admin-edited schedules (storage cleanup, chat retention, directory sync) are
saved through whichever worker serves the request, which is usually not the
leader. The leader therefore re-reads them from the database every minute
(job_refresh_dynamic_schedules); this also fixes the pre-existing drift where
only the worker that handled the admin request ever learned of the change.
auth_sync_scheduler no longer starts the scheduler on non-leaders.

Tests: tests/test_scheduler_leader.py (state machine on SQLite; exclusivity
and hand-over on PostgreSQL under RUN_POSTGRES_RESERVATION_CANARY, added to
the CI canary job).

